  "id": "false-self",
  "term": "false self",
  "definition": "In Winnicott’s object relations theory, the false self is a part of self-development understood in relation to the true self. It is used to link features of adult psychopathology with early maternal-child relationships and the quality of the person’s early facilitating environment.",
